     "answer": "Lencho is portrayed as a simple, hardworking farmer with unwavering faith in God. He is deeply devoted to his family and his crops, which are his only source of livelihood. Despite facing the devastating hailstorm that destroys his crops, Lencho does not lose hope. His faith in God is so strong that he writes a letter to Him asking for financial help. Lencho is also shown to be stubborn and somewhat naive, as he believes that God will definitely help him and is quick to accuse the post office staff of stealing when he receives less money than he asked for. However, his determination to survive and provide for his family is commendable. Overall, Lencho's character represents the resilience and faith of common people in the face of adversity."
